🧠 Advanced Tip (Very Strong Interview Point)

If your query is mostly:

WHERE role_type = 'ADMIN'
  AND created_date > '2025-09-01'

Then a better index would be:

(role_type, created_date)

Because:

First exact match on role_type

Then range on created_date

👉 This will use both columns efficiently.





🚀 Golden Rule for Composite Index Design

Order columns like this:

Equality conditions first

Range conditions after

High selectivity columns first (usually)